  "name": "GIARDIA ANTIGEN DETECTION",
  "code": "2752",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong>Test Interpretation:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>G. lamblia, is an important cause of chronic diarrhoeas world-wide.</li>\n<li>It has been commonly reported in travelers, children in day - care centers and homosexual males and is one of the most frequently identified pathogen in all waterborne outbreaks.</li>\n<li>This is a immunochromatographic test for the qualitative detection of Giardia lamblia antigen in stool samples.</li>\n<li>Sensitivity of this test is 100% and specificity is 95%.</li>\n<li>A positive result in the test depends on presence of a detectable level of antigen.</li>\n<li>A negative result can be because of intermittent excretion of the pathogen or undetectable level of antigens in the sample. If the patient is strongly suspected as being infected by Giardia, repeat testing after is advised.<br><br><br>&nbsp;</li>\n</ul>",
